  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">DLT stands for<a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-do-distributed-and-decentralized-mean\"> <strong id=\"\">distributed</strong></a><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-ledger\"> <strong id=\"\">ledger</strong></a> technology.<a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-blockchain\"> <strong id=\"\">Blockchains</strong></a> and Directed Acyclic Graphs (DAG) are examples of DLT.</p><p id=\"\">As <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-radix\"><strong id=\"\">Radix</strong></a> has a unique data structure different from blockchains (it has no blocks), Radix is called Radix DLT.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-cerberus-2\"><strong id=\"\">What is Cerberus?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-blockchain\"><strong id=\"\">What is a Blockchain?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://www.radixdlt.com/post/cerberus-infographic-series-chapter-i\"><strong id=\"\">Cerberus Infographic Series</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://www.radixdlt.com/whitepapers/consensus\"><strong id=\"\">Cerberus White Paper</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">What is a ledger?</strong></a></li></ul>",
